/* Deliberately empty.

   This file used to override CFBundleDisplayName to "MiniStore" for the Home Screen, on the
   assumption that installation_proxy reports the raw Info.plist value and a localized override
   is display-only. It does not: `get_apps` returns the *localized* CFBundleDisplayName, so the
   device reported "MiniStore".

   iLoader's get_sidestore_info (nab138/iloader, src-tauri/src/pairing.rs) calls
   `get_apps(Some("User"), None)` with no return_attributes and then matches

       if n == "SideStore" || (live_container && n == "LiveContainer")

   on that exact string, with no bundle-identifier fallback. So the override made MiniStore
   invisible to stock iLoader — it could not find the app to place a pairing file next to.

   The Home Screen and installation_proxy read the same value, so this is either/or, and
   iLoader detection wins. The name is still "MiniStore" everywhere the app controls it:
   My Apps (InstalledApp.name) and the store listing (StoreApp.makeAltStoreApp) both override
   it in code, and neither is visible to installation_proxy.

   Keep the key out of here. Adding it back breaks pairing for every stock-iLoader user. */
